# Style and Conventions

## Shell scripts (*.sh)
- Use bash; add `#!/usr/bin/env bash` when creating new scripts.
- Strict mode when reasonable: `set -Eeuo pipefail`.
- Use long flags; avoid command aliases.
- Quote variable expansions and paths.

## Kitty/Hyprland/INI-like (*.conf)
- Keep key/value on single lines; preserve spacing.
- Avoid hardcoding shells; prefer terminal defaults or `/usr/bin/zsh` if required.

## QML (*.qml)
- Favor clear property names; no inline comments inside JSON-like blocks.
- Keep components small; extract to modules under `.config/quickshell/ii/modules/` when reused.

## fish (*.fish)
- Do not introduce new fish-only bindings; provide POSIX-compatible alternatives where possible.
